WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:05.982
Search for the fabric and open its saved costing
to inspect the original figures.

2
00:00:09.200 --> 00:00:14.715
This snapshot preserves the original inputs and
results, so you can refer back to them.

3
00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:22.051
Choose Use to restore the inputs.

4
00:00:22.291 --> 00:00:25.473
Change the weaving rate to sixteen rupees per
metre.

5
00:00:33.500 --> 00:00:39.527
Set the target margin to twenty percent, then
open Live Cost to review the updated result.

6
00:00:42.500 --> 00:00:44.126
Choose Save New Version.

7
00:00:44.366 --> 00:00:49.549
Version two preserves your changes while version
one keeps its original figures.

8
00:00:53.300 --> 00:00:58.355
Enable Compare, then open the fabric's version
history to choose the estimates.

9
00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:03.946
Select versions one and two.

10
00:01:04.186 --> 00:01:08.623
You can now compare how the changed assumptions
affect the same fabric.

11
00:01:15.500 --> 00:01:17.358
Open Compare Costings.

12
00:01:17.598 --> 00:01:19.902
Review the differences in production cost,

13
00:01:20.022 --> 00:01:21.259
selling price,

14
00:01:21.379 --> 00:01:25.475
margin and quantity to understand the effect of
your changes.

15
00:01:34.000 --> 00:01:37.053
Open Export to preview an internal cost sheet.

16
00:01:43.000 --> 00:01:47.374
Enter your business name and notes, then
download the detailed cost sheet.

17
00:01:58.000 --> 00:02:00.061
Switch to Customer Quotation.

18
00:02:00.301 --> 00:02:02.822
Add the buyer’s name and delivery terms.

19
00:02:07.000 --> 00:02:11.097
Download a quote that keeps your internal costs
and margins private.
